{"name":"Calla Lily","hex":"#e4eaed","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"calla lily","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A common name for certain flowering plants in the genus Zantedeschia; not related to either the genus Calla or the true lilies (Liliaceae)","A flower of one of these plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calla_lily"}],"entries":[{"title":"Calla lily","blocks":[{"text":"Calla lily is a common name of several members of the family, Araceae. It may refer to:"},{"items":["Calla palustris","Zantedeschia generally\nZantedeschia aethiopica specifically","Zantedeschia aethiopica specifically"]},{"items":["Zantedeschia aethiopica specifically"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calla_lily"},{"title":"Calla Lily (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Calla Lily is a 2006 Philippine television drama series broadcast by ABS-CBN. Directed by Maryo J. de los Reyes and Lino Cayetano, it stars Sharlene San Pedro in the title role. It aired on the network's Primetime Bida line up from May 29 to September 8, 2006, replacing Panday and was replaced by Crazy for You."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calla_Lily_(TV_series)"},{"title":"Calla","blocks":[{"text":"Calla is a genus of flowering plant in the family Araceae, containing the single species Calla palustris. It is the only genus in the tribe Calleae of the subfamily Aroideae. Its systematic position has been described as \"puzzling\", and it has also been placed in its own family Callaceae and its own subfamily Calloideae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Calla_palustris2.jpg/330px-Calla_palustris2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calla"},{"title":"Lilium","blocks":[{"text":"Lilium is a genus of herbaceous flowering plants growing from bulbs, all with large and often prominent flowers. Lilies are a group of flowering plants which are important in culture and literature in much of the world. Most species are native to the Northern Hemisphere and their range is temperate climates and extends into the subtropics. Many other plants have \"lily\" in their common names, but do not belong to the same genus and are therefore not true lilies. True lilies are known to be highly toxic to cats."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Lilium_candidum_1.jpg/330px-Lilium_candidum_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lilium"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Illustration_Calla_palustris_clean.jpg/500px-Illustration_Calla_palustris_clean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Illustration_Calla_palustris_clean.jpg/1280px-Illustration_Calla_palustris_clean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Illustration_Calla_palustris_clean.jpg/500px-Illustration_Calla_palustris_clean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIllustration_Calla_palustris_clean.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Lillium_Stamens.jpg/500px-Lillium_Stamens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Lillium_Stamens.jpg/1280px-Lillium_Stamens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Lillium_Stamens.jpg/500px-Lillium_Stamens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lilium longiflorum flower – 1. stigma, 2. style, 3. anthers, 4. filament, 5. tepal","link":"https:/